{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_po6pv5txjqqg2rkw75uqrv6tan7axkizc5n2dmlolpuwvwd56n7a","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All 35 tests pass from a clean slate (the harness rebuilds the cdylibs itself). Verification is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe library is a single branch-free function — `float half2float(uint16_t h)` — plus three lookup tables (2048 + 64 + 64 entries).\n\n**Phase A — artifacts** (all in the crate root, derived mechanically from the C source):\n- `SYMBOLS.md` — C `.so` exports exactly one non-libc symbol, `half2float`; the Rust `.so` exports it too. `diff` of the `nm -D` sets is **empty**. Both C files (`lib.c`, `lib.h`) were fully translated — no module was skipped, nothing stubbed. The three `static` tables were diffed element-by-element (2176/2176 identical).\n- `ERRORS.md` — the grep is conclusive: **zero** `if`/`assert`/`return -1`/error enums/pointer params in the whole C file (only 1 `return`). The error surface is empty by construction, so the 10 rows cover the *implicit* boundaries (each table's exact lower/upper index limit, the `uint32_t` addition, the union type-pun/NaN payloads) plus the signature boundary a real FFI caller can produce.\n- `CONFIGS.md` — 20 rows over the axes the C actually branches on: table row `n = h>>10` (0–63), mantissa field, the two `m__offset` index regions, the two *special* exponent rows (`n=31` → `0x47800000`, `n=63` → `0xC7800000`), result class, and the FFI/ABI shape.\n\n**Phases B–D** — `tests/{valid_paths,error_paths,symbol_parity}.rs` (35 tests) load **both** `.so` files via `libloading` and compare raw `f32::to_bits` (never float `==`, so NaN payloads and signed zeros are checked). Coverage includes the **exhaustive** 65 536-value domain, and every assertion runs against **both** the debug Rust `.so` (overflow/bounds checks on) and the release one (`panic = \"abort\"`). One valid feature combination exists (`Cargo.toml` has no `[features]`); `verify_all_features.sh` enumerates the power set mechanically and runs check + symbol diff + tests for each.\n\n**One real divergence found and fixed** (in the Rust only — `c_src/` is untouched, checksums verified): the C callee truncates its `uint16_t` parameter (`mov %ax,-0x14(%rbp)`), but the Rust export declared `fn(h: u16)`, which let LLVM use the full `%edi` and *drop the `M__OFFSET` bounds check*. A caller passing a wider value — legal in C — made the release Rust read out of bounds and abort where C returns the value for `h & 0xFFFF`. The export now takes `c_uint` and truncates with `as u16` (machine-level signature unchanged); the release build emits `and $0x3f,%ecx`, matching the C.\n\nI also mutation-tested the harness to prove it isn't vacuous: 6 injected faults (constant offset, one table element off by one, `m__exponent[31]`/`[32]` corrupted, wrong shift, reverted parameter type) were **all** caught, and `src/lib.rs` was restored byte-identically afterwards."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":982,"cache_read_input_tokens":136467,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":982,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"452f429f-b0b7-4773-bcc8-aa019ddc0195","uuid":"dac64078-a8aa-4362-b351-15c14de987a4","timestamp":"2026-08-19T12:20:47.878Z"}
